<para>Represents a temperature and provides conversions and operations between scales. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="class_temperature" kindref="compound">Temperature</ref> class manages a temperature value expressed in three scales: Celsius, Fahrenheit, and Kelvin. It supports arithmetic and comparison operators, as well as serialization via Boost archives.</para>
<para>Example usage: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="class_temperature_1afe68f33b2cb48f1bd2c6a7d94ffa9d6c" kindref="member">Temperature</ref><sp/>t1(25.0);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="class_temperature_1afe68f33b2cb48f1bd2c6a7d94ffa9d6c" kindref="member">Temperature</ref><sp/>t2(10.0);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="class_temperature_1afe68f33b2cb48f1bd2c6a7d94ffa9d6c" kindref="member">Temperature</ref><sp/>result<sp/>=<sp/>t1<sp/>+<sp/>t2;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">std::cout<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/>result.<ref refid="class_temperature_1a43c7c2285c4eedb6fb50f449400f43c9" kindref="member">getTemperatureCelsius</ref>()<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/>std::endl;</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
